    "https://brevard.edu/career%20advantage/": {
      "title": "Brevard Career Advantage",
      "description": "Brevard College Career Advantage | Brevard College Skip to content Academics Majors Minors & Concentrations Undergraduate Research Conference Graduate Programs Graduation Information Brevard Career Advantage Honors Program Find Your Career Path Admissions & Aid Apply for Admission Apply for Scholarships & Aid Confirm My Offer of Admission (Direct Admission) Pay My Enrollment Fee Register for a Scholarship Competition Register for Student Orientation Advising and Registration (S.O.A.R!) Schedule My Campus Visit Tuition & Fees Forms Campus Life Campus Life Graduation Information Clubs & Student Involvement New Student Center Student Success Career Services Outdoor Adventures The Town of Brevard Athletics Campus Ministry Institute for Women in Leadership Residence Life & Dorms Alumni & Friends Make a Gift Annual Fund Planned Giving New Student Center Donor Recognition Alumni Association Refer a Student About Brevard Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) Brevard at a Glance Brevard Career Advantage Remarkable Outcomes New Student Center News Events Campus Map The Porter Center for the Performing Arts The J.A. Jones Library & ELC Contact Us Directory Post a Job or Internship Career Opportunities at Brevard Apply Visit Direct Admission Scholarships Pay My Enrollment Fee Make a Gift Apply Visit Pay My Enrollment Fee Pay My Bill Give Athletics MyBrevard News Apply Visit Pay My Enrollment Fee Pay My Bill Give Athletics MyBrevard News Menu Brevard Career Advantage Your future is our passion. Your success is our purpose. The Brevard Career Advantage is a four-year individualized and adaptive career roadmap that leads each student to their desired career and post-college life. Brevard Career Advantage An Individualized, Adaptable Road Map for Every Student This program originated in an academic department. The success was overwhelming.  For those students engaged in this program over the past decade, almost 100% left Brevard College employed in their field of choice, or attending a graduate school of their choosing. Of those students who chose to go on to graduate studies, most attended with full-ride scholarships or graduate fellowships. That proven success has led to taking the program campus-wide and naming it Brevard Career Advantage. What makes Brevard Career Advantage so successful? The faculty at Brevard College are passionate about helping each student discover themselves, their career and their purpose. Every semester of a student’s time at Brevard College is partially engaged with creating and adjusting this roadmap. It is embedded in our curriculum in every major. It is central to our relationships. It is part of our culture. How does Brevard College do this? We commit ourselves to it. We do this by prioritizing relationships, experiences, mentoring, and individualized care. The Brevard Career Advantage starts when students arrive on campus their first year. They begin working with a personal advisor and First-Year Experience instructor. This process continues every semester until graduation. This effectively ensures that students are as well-positioned as possible for a career and life of success, meaning, achievement, and happiness. Results This program gets results. \"The unending support from my faculty for letter writing, phone calls about jobs, references, and resume editing is the only reason that I received the positions I'm in now.\" - Alex, MFA, Theatre Performance & Pedagogy 99% of Students Engaged in this program have been employed in their field of choice. Active Engagement Most colleges offer career services and career checklists. These approaches are passive. This program is different. It is an active commitment to an individualized, adaptive career road map for each and every student. How It Works Building Your Personalized Career Roadmap The Brevard Career Advantage means we’re here to support you every step of the way as you build a future you’re passionate about. Here’s a look at what you can expect in each year of your Brevard College journey: Year 1: Discover & Connect Your first year is all about getting connected—both to campus life and to the direction you want to take in your career. You’ll work one-on-one with your advisor to identify your strengths, explore different educational pathways, and find ways to get involved with the community. This is the time to discover your passions and start building a foundation for success. Personalized advising to discuss career interests and strengths Access to campus and community resources Support in discovering purpose and potential career pathways Year 2: Define Your Direction As you move into your second year, we’ll guide you in shaping a clearer vision of your future. Together, we’ll continue to design a personalized plan of courses and experiences that align with your goals and give you the expertise to stand out in your field. Tailored course planning with advisors to build relevant knowledge Opportunities to gain field-specific experience Creation of a personalized portfolio to highlight expertise and skills Year 3: Practice & Engage In your third year, it’s time to apply what you’ve learned and see it in action. You’ll engage with mentors, take on real-world challenges, and work with potential employers—on campus and beyond. This year is all about putting your skills to the test and developing the confidence to pursue your ambitions after graduation. Real-world experiences through internships and co-op placements Access to mentors and industry professionals Skill-building and practical applications of academic knowledge Year 4: Launch with Confidence Your final year at Brevard is all about preparation for what’s next. You’ll work closely with faculty and advisors to fine-tune your resume, craft professional communications, and prepare for interviews. We’ll help you make meaningful connections with potential employers and provide support as you organize applications, refine your presentations, and get ready for what lies ahead. Intensive support for job applications and graduate school admissions Networking events to connect with industry leaders and alumni Opportunities to engage with potential employers and mentors \"We recognize that College means something different for each individual. We embrace individuality and seek to encourage each student to find a path that will help them succeed.\" -President Brad Andrews \"My professor sat down with me, and helped me figure out what I want to do. Then, she worked with me on classes and internships to help me get there.\" -Ollie, Brevard College Student \"Dr. Brown in the History program helped me get an internship with the Great Smoky Mountains Association. That internship not only helped me learn more about the Parks Service, it solidified my decision to work there. It's my dream job!\" -Reagan, Brevard College Student Faculty Who Care Our College-Wide Commitment to Your Career Success For those of us who work at Brevard College, this is not only our passion, we also view it as a central component of our job. All faculty and staff are committed to this program, to student success, and to positioning each and every student for the post-college life that most inspires them. Brevard Career Advantage is more than an app, more than an office, and more than a person. It is a campus-wide, one-on-one commitment to career development and success. Do You Have 15 Minutes? Apply for Admission You are more than a test score. The application is test-optional, FREE , and only takes 15 minutes to fill out. Apply for Free Today! Visit Brevard Register for an Open House! Tour campus, chat with current students, and speak with a financial aid advocate. Schedule Your Visit! Committed to Affordability Full-Tuition Scholarships Compete for the Full-Tuition, earn other scholarships, and get your FAFSA questions answered at the next Scholarship Competition! Register for the Scholarship Competition! The land of Waterfalls Live and Learn You'll find a caring community surrounded by an incredible natural environment. There's no better place to study the sciences. Life on Campus One Brevard College Dr. Brevard, NC 28712 828.641.0641 admissions@brevard.edu (opens in new tab) (opens in new tab) (opens in new tab) Brevard College is consistently recognized as one of the best liberal arts colleges. The College's focus on experiential learning, small class sizes, and location in the mountains of Western North Carolina near Asheville make Brevard a top choice college for students around the world. Consumer Disclosure Terms of Use Title IX Privacy Policy Whistleblower Policy MyBrevard © 2026 Brevard College This institution is an equal opportunity provider. Want to learn more? Sign up to download our quick fact sheet & stay up to date with Brevard College! Footer Interest Capture First Name * Last Name * Email * Graduating Year * If you are human, leave this field blank. Request Δ"
    },
